{%- comment -%}
  Quick view — the overlay shell.

  Empty until something is asked for. theme.js fetches
  `<product url>?section_id=quick-view` and swaps the rendered panel in, exactly
  as the search overlay fetches sections/predictive-search.liquid. Nothing about
  the piece is assembled in the browser; the panel is Liquid's rendering of the
  product, so money, translation and image sizing stay where they belong.

  Rendered by sections/header.liquid, because it belongs to the cards that open
  it and every template shares the header group.

  A full-viewport overlay root must never carry a colour scheme class — that
  paints the whole screen opaque and the veil has nothing left to veil. The
  scheme goes on the panel.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="overlay overlay--quick" data-overlay="quick-view" data-overlay-modal hidden>
  <button class="overlay__veil" type="button" data-overlay-close="quick-view">
    <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'navigation.close' | t }}</span>
  </button>

  <div
    class="quick-view scheme-{{ settings.quick_view_color_scheme }}"
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-label="{{ 'products.quick_view' | t }}"
    data-quick-view-panel
  >
    {%- comment -%}
      Named as the focus target explicitly: the veil is also a close control and
      comes first in the document, so without this the overlay would open with
      focus on a full-screen invisible button.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button
      class="quick-view__close"
      type="button"
      data-overlay-close="quick-view"
      data-overlay-autofocus
      data-tip="{{ 'navigation.close' | t }}"
    >
      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'navigation.close' | t }}</span>
      <span aria-hidden="true">&#10005;</span>
    </button>

    <div class="quick-view__contents" data-quick-view-contents></div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Shown while the panel is on its way. The overlay opens on the click rather
      than on the response, so the piece is never a wait with nothing on screen.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="quick-view__loading" data-quick-view-loading>
      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.quick_view_loading' | t }}</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
